      "id": "2027-Equi-12-3",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Equities Mod12-Q3",
        "itemBody": "<p>Gableton is a privately held mining company based in Australia with properties producing gold, silver, and copper. An analyst is assessing the potential for Gableton in the IPO market and has created a set of 10 comparable publicly traded mining companies in Australia. The beta estimate for an equally weighted portfolio of these 10 companies is 0.65. The average ratio of debt to market capitalization across the 10 companies is 40%, and the average tax rate is 30%. Gableton’s ratio of debt to estimated market value of equity is 60%, and its tax rate is 25%. Which of the following is closest to the analyst’s estimate of Gableton’s beta?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "1bf8c5d3-9907-4e4a-99a1-3a31308f39fc",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. 0.51</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "606c1c9d-2d3c-4a1f-9469-98b6f17d0a1f",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. 0.74</p>",
              "position": 2
